          "text": "The claim oversimplifies. Mild intellectual disability (IQ ~50-70) involves challenges in reasoning, problem-solving, and abstract thinking, which can lead to relying on others for help, like asking questions instead of independent deep thought. However, \"refusing to think\" implies unwillingness, not inability. Asking questions often shows curiosity, which many sources link to higher intelligence. It's not a definitive low-IQ trait. Sources: APA, Wikipedia, psychology articles."
